  "prompt": "Image 1 is the exact character identity and art reference: Noct final six-star form, a chibi GRIM REAPER in clean HD smooth painted game art (NOT pixel art). Keep him exactly: deep near-black hood that swallows all detail, the face completely hidden in darkness with ONLY two tiny luminous cold pale-violet eyes visible; long compact torn layered black robe with ragged tattered edges, extremely subtle deep-charcoal folds; small dark boots; ONE single classic Death scythe with a long plain dark shaft and ONE large elongated curved pale silver reaping blade with a restrained cold violet/silver edge, mounted at the top of the shaft. NO shiny armour, NO silver chest plates, NO belt ornaments, NO visible face or skin, NO body rim light, NO twin blades, NO double-ended weapon, NO crescent staff. Overall reads as ominous living darkness where only the eyes and the scythe are easy to discern.\nImage 2 is a scale-and-root template made from the same accepted character. Preserve Image 2 exact cell locations, fixed camera distance, standing-equivalent anatomical scale, body-root position at the horizontal center of each cell, grounded foot-contact line at about 94% of cell height, and padding. Change only the action pose in each slot. Never zoom or resize a pose to fill its cell. Hood, torso, robe, boots and scythe size must stay identical to Image 2 in every frame. Do not reproduce Image 2 as-is and do not draw any guide, border or separator.\n\nCreate a 6-frame RUN loop animation sheet, body only: a grounded ominous gliding run cycle moving RIGHT. The reaper leans forward, scythe carried diagonally close behind his shoulder with the blade tucked above and behind the hood, legs alternating stride with boots touching the ground line in contact frames, torn robe tatters trailing back to the left but kept short enough to stay inside the cell. Frame 1: right foot contact. Frame 2: push-off, body slightly lower. Frame 3: passing pose, body slightly higher. Frame 4: left foot contact. Frame 5: push-off. Frame 6: passing pose, loops back to frame 1. Torso stays near cell center; no whole-body horizontal travel across the cell.\n\nFacing RIGHT in 3/4 view in every frame. Body plus scythe only: NO detached slash arc, NO weapon trail, NO motion lines, NO particles, NO sparks, NO smoke clouds, NO aura, NO wisps, NO magic circle (aura smoke is a separate runtime layer). Keep the scythe compact and close to the body so it stays fully inside its own cell: the blade may rise above the hood but must never cross any cell edge; leave a clear magenta margin of at least 5% on all four sides of every cell. Same camera distance and same body scale in all 6 frames; body center stays near the cell center; feet stay on the same ground line except where noted.\nExactly 6 frames in a 3 columns x 2 rows grid of equal square 512x512 cells, total image 1536x1024, read left-to-right then next row. Background 100% solid flat #FF00FF magenta in every cell, no gradient, no floor, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no numbers, no gridlines, no borders, no frames between cells. Clean HD smooth painted, NOT pixel art.\n",
